{"id":"extra","lemma":"extra","pos":"adv","rank":1544,"glosses":["specifically (for a given purpose)","on purpose","aside, apart, separately"],"ipa":"/ˈɛks.tʁa/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/e1/De-at-extra.ogg/De-at-extra.ogg.mp3","examples":[{"text":"Du brauchst nicht extra aufzustehen.","en":"You don't need to stand up.","words":[{"g":"you"},{"g":"to need","l":"brauchen"},{"g":"not"},null,{"g":"to get up (move from a…","l":"aufstehen"}]},{"text":"Die Batterien muss man extra bezahlen.","en":"You need to pay extra for the batteries.","words":[{"g":"the"},{"g":"battery","l":"Batterie"},{"g":"to have to","l":"müssen"},{"g":"one"},null,{"g":"to pay"}]},{"text":"Die Lautsprecher werden extra verkauft.","en":"The speakers are sold separately.","words":[{"g":"the"},{"g":"loudspeaker"},{"g":"to become"},null,{"g":"sold"}]},{"text":"Übergepäck kostet viel extra.","en":"Excess baggage costs a lot extra.","words":[null,{"g":"to cost","l":"kosten"},{"g":"much, a lot"},null]},{"text":"Ich weiß, dass Tom das extra gemacht hat.","en":"I know Tom did it on purpose.","words":[{"g":"I"},{"g":"to know","l":"wissen"},{"g":"that"},null,{"g":"the / that"},null,{"g":"to make","l":"machen"},{"g":"has","l":"haben"}]}]}